WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.030
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Welcome to Blog two, implementing Pattern A high-density pooled multi-tenancy on Cloud Run and BigQuery.

2
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:20.053
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Our pooled Cloud Run runtime uses the second-generation execution environment with single-request concurrency per container instance.

3
00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:30.083
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: In BigQuery Studio, querying the shared pooled table under the operator baseline displays records across competing tenants.

4
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:40.106
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Notice seven combined rows from FinVault, Globex, MedCore, and RetailStream appearing together in the same grid.

5
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:50.136
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Inspecting native row-level access policies displays our FinVault tenant filter predicate active directly inside BigQuery.

6
00:00:50.136 --> 00:01:00.159
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Cloud Logging records the pooled service account running parameterized tenant queries layered above our row access policy.

7
00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:10.189
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: To stop noisy neighbors from exhausting shared quotas, Firestore tracks live per-tenant request budgets across the pool.

8
00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:20.212
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Exceeding a tenant threshold triggers deterministic rate-limit throttling while protecting latency for every other customer.

9
00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:30.242
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Extending Pattern A into Databricks Lakehouse, querying our unfiltered pooled table initially exposes all competing tenants together.

10
00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:40.265
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Without Unity Catalog row filters enabled, a shared SQL warehouse credential risks exposing unauthorized records across customer tenants.

11
00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:50.295
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Inspecting Databricks Catalog Explorer confirms our active Unity Catalog row filter policy bound directly onto the pooled table.

12
00:01:50.295 --> 00:02:00.318
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Re-running the identical query without any filter clause returns strictly authorized FinVault records with zero foreign tenant bleed.
